# No static certificates here (unlike the techhanker.com host's tls.yml,
# which references mkcert/manually-issued cert files) -- every host on this
# deployment gets a cert on-demand from whichever resolver is selected (see
# traefik.yaml.tftpl and locals.tf acme_cert_resolver, referenced by the
# per-router certResolver: ${acme_cert_resolver} entries in the other
# dynamic-*.yaml files).
#
# KNOWN ISSUE (investigated 2026-08-21, unresolved): on this deployment,
# Traefik's DNS-01 resolver (ionos) correctly registers with Let's Encrypt
# and successfully issues real certs -- confirmed by extracting and
# `openssl x509`-verifying the stored cert for saas.riogentix.com directly
# from acme-ionos.json (valid Let's Encrypt cert, correct SANs). DEBUG logs
# also confirm the cert is loaded into Traefik's runtime certificate store
# ("Adding certificate for domain(s) saas.riogentix.com",
# "No ACME certificate generation required for domains"). Despite that,
# every live TLS handshake -- tested from the VM's own loopback with native
# openssl s_client, ruling out the STACKIT load balancer or any external
# network path -- still receives the static self-signed "TRAEFIK DEFAULT
# CERT" that ships baked into the Traefik binary. Ruled out: TLS store
# naming, custom tls.options vs. none at all, Traefik v3.1.7 vs. v3.5.6,
# stale/duplicate containers on port 443 (confirmed single docker-proxy
# listener), acme.json file permissions (600, root-owned, as required).
# Tried and also failed: explicit tls.stores.default.defaultGeneratedCert
# pointing at the ionos resolver (the documented fix for the general
# "no default certificate" class of Traefik issue) -- it either 500s with
# "unable to find certificate for domains" against a cert that
# demonstrably exists with matching main+sans, or silently has no effect.
# This matches multiple long-standing, still-open upstream Traefik
# community threads about ACME certs being obtained but not served over
# TLS in v2 and v3 alike. Needs either an upstream Traefik bug report or a
# deeper runtime trace (pprof/strace) to pin down further -- next person
# picking this up should start there rather than re-deriving the above.
tls:
  options:
    default:
      minVersion: VersionTLS12
      cipherSuites:
        - TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256
        - TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256
        - TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384
        - TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384
        - TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_CHACHA20_POLY1305
        - TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_CHACHA20_POLY1305
